A||||10||billfredmike24||Sunroof sealing?||||1||
Z||000000||billfredmike24||08-20-2001||12:42 AM||||I installed a stock sunroof in my car and was wondering when you close it, is it supposed to "snap" shut to make a good seal?  Mine doesn't and by looking at the gap it seems i'm gonna get a lot of rain in it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_10.jpg"> <BR>yeah the wheels are ugly, and the stickers, that'll change||||reg||1
Z||000001||billfredmike24||08-20-2001||12:02 PM||||Nobody ever open or close their sunroofs? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||08-20-2001||12:06 PM||||Mine closes nice and tight. It can be adjusted by loosening the latch assembly where it is attached to the frame of the car and moving it back a little.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||3
Z||000003||fierobaby||08-20-2001||12:09 PM||||BillfredMike,<P>Hey I have a suunroof and I also have a gap...or had one... you really need to make sure that your tabs are shoved in all the way which isn't the easiest thing to do if you have rusty tabs... what you do is pop up your sunroof like you are just gonna prop it up. get out of the car and push the back of the sunroof you may have to jiggle it a bit then climb back in and close it the gap should have become smaller if not... cover your interiour with something that will absorb water and shoot water at the roof and see if it leaks||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||08-20-2001||12:13 PM||||You can remove the latch and ad washers between it and the roof to pull the roof down tighter. Also keeping the seal clean with armour all or simular product. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||cadaver||08-21-2001||10:57 PM||||there are spacer pads that go under the latch. Mine only had one so I installed another one, now its good. You should also drill the drain holes if they are not already there.||||reg||1
Z||000006||billfredmike24||08-21-2001||11:47 PM||||Drain hole?? can you give me more info. on this please<BR>Thanks Mike||||reg||1
Z||000007||RossT||08-21-2001||11:55 PM||||Do a search for drain holes, about a month ago someone posted some great pics of an 85 and where the drain holes need to be drilled.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Galen||08-22-2001||12:08 AM||||Drain holes are mucho importanto..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> mine leaked like a ... waterfall and now it dont after drilling them there holes<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">  Ray -    <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000009||DecadenceR||08-22-2001||03:00 AM||||Drain holes are really easy, I did it on my 84 (R.I.P.)<P>Take out the sunroof glass. In each corner pull back the seal, and drill a hole as close to the raised corner (towards interior, exactly opposite of the seal) as you can. Then vaccum.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||billfredmike24||08-22-2001||11:46 AM||||I searched for drain holes and brought the thread back up in tech. section.  The pictures no longer show up, anyone have pictures of exactly where i drill.<BR>Thanks Mike||||reg||1
